I was playing (in wizard mode) a neutral Priest wearing a helm
of opposite alignment to make him chaotic.  When I went to the
altar at the start of the quest level (an unaligned altar to Moloch)
and sacrificed, I got the following message:


Your sacrifice is consumed in a burst of flame!
You sense a conflict between Huan Ti and Moloch.
Unluckily, you feel the power of Huan Ti decrease.  unaligned player?--More--
Program in disorder - perhaps you'd better Quit.--More--
The voice of Moloch booms:  "Thou shalt pay for thy indiscretion!"--More--
The horned devil of Moloch appears before you.--More--
The trident welds itself to the horned devil of Moloch's hand!--More--
...
and then the game continued.

Not really too severe a bug.  The "summon minion" routine just doesn't
accomodate sacrifices at non-aligned altars too well.
